  "description": "Thirteen alternating red and white stripes with a navy canton bearing twenty-one white five-pointed stars in four rows of 5, 4, 6 and 6.",
  "history": "The 21-star flag became official on 4 July 1819 after the admission of Illinois, under the Flag Act of 1818 which fixed the stripes at thirteen and added a star for each new state on the following Fourth of July. It was superseded on 4 July 1820 by the 23-star flag for Alabama and Maine.",
